ANALYSIS 5: Break-Even Math
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
COST = $2.4000000000000004, WIN = $3.54, LOSS = $-2.4000000000000004
Break-even WR = 40.40%

For positive EV, you need:
  WR × $3.54 + (1-WR) × $-2.40 > 0
  WR > 0.4040 = 40.4%

Current simulated WR: ~32-33% (under fair-value assumption)
Required uplift: +7-8 percentage points

Where could this come from?
  A. Polymarket inefficiency (oracle lag → token mispriced)
  B. Slow-fill capture (you fill at 0.40 when fair was 0.50)
  C. Real BTC has stronger AR(1) than -0.05 (mean reversion)
  D. Time-of-day liquidity gaps (low volume hours)


